"51.Rxd5 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 86% to 7%.","points":["Black answers 51…Qxe1+, which takes the rook on e1.","After Qxe1+, Black wins 1 point of material within 4 moves.","Better was 51.Rb4 (+4.99), which attacks the b3 pawn, which is undefended."],"better":"51.Rb4 wins a pawn, picking it up with 52.Rxb3, and threatens Rb8+, winning a bishop, picking it up with 52.Rxe8+. After 51…Rc8 52.Rxb3 Re8 53.Rb4 Qf5 54.Rd4, White comes out a pawn up (+4.99)."},{"ply":102,"name":"51…Qxe1+","cls":"brilliant","color":"b","headline":"51…Qxe1+!! A real sacrifice: Black gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the queen on e1 where it can be taken.","White can take, but after 52.Qxe1 Bxd5 53.Qd2 Re6 the engine rates it −8.82.","Takes the rook on e1.","51…Qxe1+ wins a rook for a queen.","Takes the rook on e1 and wins a rook for a queen once the captures settle.","White answers 52.Qxe1, taking back and attacking the e2 pawn, which is undefended."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"51…Qxe1+!! offers the queen on e1. Taking it gives Black the material back and more."},{"title":"What Black gives up","text":"51…Qxe1+ puts the queen on e1 where it can be taken by the queen on d2. That's the queen on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It takes the rook on e1. The rook on e1 was the only piece guarding a1 and b1 next to White's king."},{"title":"If White takes the queen","text":"52.Qxe1 is met by 52…Bxd5, taking the rook on d5. Then 53…Be4+ gives check, and 54…Bf3 threatens mate. Black ends up two pawns ahead: Black is winning (−7.60). This is White's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 51…Re6, is clearly weaker (+6.39 against −8.82). White answers 52.Rd8+. That would leave Black losing."}]},{"ply":119,"name":"60.Qd1","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"60.Qd1 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 50% to 8%.","points":["Black answers 60…Rh4, which protects the b3 pawn, which was hanging.","Better was 60.Qe3 (0.00): the queen joins the attack: it now hits 4 squares around the Black king."],"better":"60.Qe3 stops …Rh4. Engine line: 60…Re4 61.Qb6+ Kd7 62.Qf2 Ra4+ 63.Kb1 (0.00)."},{"ply":123,"name":"62.Kc1","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"62.Kc1 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 50% to 6%.","points":["Black answers 62…Ra1+: the rook forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","After Ra1+, Black wins 4 points of material within 5 moves.","Better was 62.Qe2 (0.00): activates the queen (from 13 to 19 usable squares)."],"better":"62.Qe2 threatens Qe8+, winning a rook, picking it up with 63.Qxa4, and stops …Be4+. Engine line: 62…Rc4 63.Qe8+ Kc7 64.Qe5+ Kc6 (0.00)."},{"ply":124,"name":"62…Kb5","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"62…Kb5 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 94% to 3%.","points":["White answers 63.Qxd5+, which takes the bishop on d5.","After Qxd5+, White wins 3 points of material within 2 moves.","Better was 62…Ra1+ (−7.56): the rook forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once."],"better":"62…Ra1+ wins the queen for a rook, picking it up with 63…Rxd1+. After 63.Kd2 Rxd1+ 64.Kxd1 Bc4 65.Kd2 Kd5, Black comes out a piece and a pawn up (−7.56)."},{"ply":125,"name":"63.Kd2","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"63.Kd2 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 97% to 7%.","points":["Black answers 63…Rd4+, which skewers the king: when it moves, the queen on d1 behind it falls.","After Rd4+, Black wins 5 points of material within 6 moves.","Better was 63.Qxd5+ (+9.15), which takes the bishop on d5."],"better":"63.Qxd5+ wins a bishop for a pawn and forks the king and the pawn. After 63…Kb4 64.Qb7+ Kxa5 65.Qa7+ Kb5 66.Qd7+, White comes out two pawns up (+9.15)."},{"ply":126,"name":"63…Be4","cls":"miss","color":"b","headline":"63…Be4 misses 63…Rd4+, which wins material. Black's winning chances go from 93% to 8%.","points":["White answers 64.Qxb3+, which takes the pawn on b3.","Better was 63…Rd4+ (−6.92), which skewers the king: when it moves, the queen on d1 behind it falls."],"better":"63…Rd4+ wins the queen for a rook, picking it up with 64…Rxd1+. After 64.Ke1 Rxd1+ 65.Kxd1 Kxa5 66.Ke1 Kb6, Black comes out the exchange plus a pawn up (−6.92)."}],"opening":{"name":"French Defense: Steinitz Variation, Boleslavsky Variation","eco":"C11","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 11…Qa5: 22 moves in all, 11 by White and 11 by Black.","Theory runs out after 11…Qa5: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}